{"ticker":"GLENMARK","symbol":"GLENMARK","instrumentId":3022914,"name":"Glenmark Pharma.","industry":"NSE-Medical-Generic Drugs","about":"Glenmark Pharmaceuticals Ltd. is a global pharmaceutical company, focused on innovation in the areas of respiratory, dermatology, and oncology. With a presence in over 80 countries, the company operates 10 manufacturing facilities across five continents. Glenmark offers a wide range of branded, generics, and over-the-counter (OTC) products, driven by a strong commitment to research and development. The company collaborates with its U.S. subsidiary Ichnos Sciences through the 'Ichnos Glenmark Innovation' initiative to advance cancer treatment. Glenmark’s dual strategy of developing innovative drugs and specialty products, such as RYALTRIS®, continues to challenge treatment paradigms and improve patient outcomes globally.","website":"www.glenmarkpharma.com","location":"Mumbai, INDIA","exchange":"NSE","fetchedAt":"2026-11-20T13:22:27.551Z","basis":"consolidated","price":{"value":2608.5,"changePct":-1.420959147424508,"week52High":2677.2,"week52Low":1842.4},"stats":[{"label":"Market capitalization","value":"₹73,618 Cr"},{"label":"Sales","value":"₹15,937 Cr"},{"label":"Shares in float","value":"149,579,000"},{"label":"No. of funds","value":"499"},{"label":"Shares held by funds","value":"110,470,783"},{"label":"Dividend yield","value":"0.10%"},{"label":"Book value","value":"7"},{"label":"U/D vol ratio","value":"1.4"},{"label":"LTDebt / equity","value":"6.0%"},{"label":"Alpha","value":"0.15"},{"label":"Beta","value":"0.97"},{"label":"EPS growth rate","value":"-24%"},{"label":"P/E ratio","value":"50.72"},{"label":"5-year P/E range","value":"13–75"},{"label":"Return on equity","value":"13.0%"},{"label":"Cash flow (INR)","value":"122.08"},{"label":"Volume","value":"536,530"},{"label":"Avg volume (50d)","value":"719,244"},{"label":"Master score","value":"58"},{"label":"EPS rating","value":"28"},{"label":"Price strength","value":"81"},{"label"